      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14213809/assets/cd878559d6be37faa60bdb33cbebe2f124d09744aa4df7dae40372499116f239.png)\n\nWhat is the length of $\\overset{―}{CD}?$",
      "worked_solution": "From the figure, we note that the points $C$ and $D$ have coordinates ${{(-5,3)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(2,-1)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})},$ respectively.\n\nTo find the length of $\\overset{―}{CD},$ we use the distance formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-(-5))^{2}+(-1-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(7)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{65}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
